  "raw_text": "204\n\nRug munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto fornicate with someone, to commit immorality with someone, to commit adultery with\nsomeone\n \n/ fornicar con alguien, cometer inmoralidad con alguien, cometer adulterio con alguien\n\nRug takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto fornicate, to commit immorality, to commit adultery\n \n/ fornicar, cometer inmoralidad, cometer\nadulterio\n\nTahkia wal prawaia l\nâ\nka\n \n(a/t:\n \nTahkia wal rug takaia l\nâ\nka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nhomosexuality\n \n/ homosexualidad\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlff\n-\n41\n):\n \n¿Gâd ba waitna apia kaka mairin ai tahkia wal prawaia brinka bri nani ra baman saura kaikisa ki?\n \n–\n\nDoes God see\n \nhomosexual desires as the only wrong ones?\n \n/ ¿Dios considera que los deseos homosexuales son\n\nlos únicos deseos\n \nmalos\n?\n)\n\nRul munaia\n \n(\ndictu\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto rule\n \n/ gobernar\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nAimakaia, King aimakaia\n)\n\nRum\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nrum, liquor\n \n/ ron, licor\n\nRum dadira\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \ndrinker of liquor, drunk\n \n/ bebedor de licor, borracho\n\nRum diaia lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nalcoholism\n \n/ alcoholismo\n\nRum diaia albika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nalcoholic\n \n/ alcohólico\n\nRûm\n \n(Rum)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nroom\n \n/ habitación\n\nRungkaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nRuhmkaia\n,\n \nRunhkaia\n,\n \nRuhkaia\n,\n \nRuhmkaia\n) (v-trans; intrans:\n \nRungwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto sink, to submerge, to dive, to\nimmerse, to plunge, to dip\n \n/ hundirse, sumergirse\n\nRungwaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nRuhmwaia\n,\n \nRunhwaia\n,\n \nRuhmaia\n) (v-intrans; trans:\n \nRungkaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto sink, to submerge, to dive, to\nimmerse, to dip\n \n/ hundirse, sumergirse\n\nRungwi tiwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto drown\n \n/ ahogar\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nKwapi pruaia\n)\n\nRup\n \n(a/t:\n \nRop\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nrope\n \n/ cuerda\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nKiwa\n)\n\nRuskika\n \n(a/t:\n \nRoskika, Uruskika\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nmonkey\n \n/ mono, mico\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nUrus\n)\n\nRut\n \n(\ndb,dba,bw,dbta\n)\n \n–\n \nRuth\n \n(Bible book) / Rut (libro bíblico)\n\nSa\n \n(v-3p-pres of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \nis, are, it is, must\n \n/ es, está, debe\n\nSâ\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsaw\n \n/ serrucho, sierra\n\nSâ wal klakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cut with a saw\n \n/ cortar con una sierra\n\nSâ ni klakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cut with a saw\n \n/ cortar con una sierra\n\nSabaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto stab, to nail, to strike, to puncture\n \n/ apuñalar, clavar, golpear, pinchar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb32\n):\n \nJael...tint watla dusa tatwa kum wal lal ra saban, bara witin pruan\n \n–\n \nJael...stabbed (him) in the head with a pointy\ntent peg, and he died\n \n/ Jael...lo clavó en la cabeza con una estaca de tienda puntiaguda y murió)\n\nAmar sabaia\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nto hammer\n \n/ martillar\n\nSabi ikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto kill by stabbing, to kill by being struck, to kill by being shot, to kill by being nailed\n \n/ matar\napuñalando, matar a golpes, matar de un tiro, matar al ser clavado\n\n(Note/Nota: It is used to refer to how Jesus was killed / Se usa para referirse a cómo Jesús fue asesinado)\n\nWalpa ni sabi ikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto kill with a stone/stones, to stone\n \n/ matar con una piedra/piedras, apedrear\n\nSabi paman\n \n–\n \nnailed and hung\n \n/ clavado y colgado\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmy41\n)\n:\n \nJisas ra dus kum ra sabi\n \npaman\n \n–\n \nJesus nailed and hung on a tree\n \n/ Jesús clavado y colgado de un\n \nmadero\n)\n\nSabat\n \n–\n \nSabbath\n \n/\n \ns\nábado\n\n(\nNote/Nota\n:\n \ndb\n \nuses\n \nRis yua\n,\n \nRis briaia yua\n,\n \nYua 7 ba\n \nand\n \nSabat\n;\n \nsln\n \nuses\n \nRest briaia yua ba\n \nin the superscription before\n \nLawana\n\nNani\n \n92;\n \nbw\n \nuses\n \nRest briaia yua ba\n \nand\n,\n \nin the first instance\n,\n \nputs\n \nSabat yua ba\n \nin brackets;\n \nlrw\n \nuses\n \nSabat\n \n63 times;\n \ndba\n \nuses\n\nSabat\n \na\n \nfew\n \ntimes\n \nbut in most cases,\n \nWingka puhbaia yua\n \nis used;\n \ndbta\n \nuses\n \nRis briaia yua\n \nand\n \nRis yua\n \nin the Hebrew scriptures\n\nand\n \nRes yua\n \nin the Greek scriptures;\n \nbh\n \nand\n \nmwb\n \nuse\n \nSabat\n \n/\n \ndb\n \nusa\n \nRis yua\n,\n \nRis briaia yua\n,\n \nYua 7 ba\n \ny\n \nSabat\n;\n \nsln\n \nusa\n \nRest briaia\n\nyua ba\n \nen la inscripción antes del\n \nLawana Nani\n \n92;\n \nbw\n \nusa\n \nRest briaia yua ba\n \ny, en primera instancia, pone entre paréntesis a\n\nSabat yua ba\n;\n \nlrw\n \nusa\n \nSabat\n \n63 veces;\n \ndba\n \nusa\n \nSabat\n \nalgunas veces, pero en la mayoría de los casos,\n \nse\n \nusa\n \nWingka puhbaia yua\n;\n\ndbta\n \nusa\n \nRis briaia yua\n \ny\n \nRis yua\n \nen las escrituras hebreas y\n \nRes yua\n \nen las escrituras griegas;\n \nbh\n \ny\n \nmwb\n \nusan\n \nSabat\n)\n\nSabat ba kulkaia\n \n(\ndb-Impakan Sturka 31:16\n)\n \n–\n \nto keep the Sabbath, to respect the Sabbath\n \n/ guardar el sábado,\nrespetar el sábado\n\nSabat lâka\n \n(a/t:\n \nSabat yua\n \nlâka\n,\n \nRis yua lâka\n)\n \n–\n \nSabbath law\n \n/ ley sabática\n\nSabat yua\n \n–\n \nSabbath day\n \n/\n \ndía\n \nde descanso\n,\n \ndía sabático\n\nS\nâ\nbi\n \n(adv)\n \n–\n \nsecretly\n \n/ secretamente\n\n(Note/Nota: Not commonly used / No se usa comúnmente)\n\nS\nâ\nbi kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto spy\n \n/ espiar\n \n(See also/\n \nV\ner también:\n \nBiki kaikaia\n)",
